  </sharedProfiles><sharedRules><rule name="Divine Pronouncement" id="4957-590d-f58b-9e0f" hidden="false">
      <description>Instead of firing a weapon in the Shooting phase the psyker can take a psychic test to use this power. Designate a single enemy unit within 18" and not in close combat. This unit must take a Morale check as if it has just suffered 25% casualties from shooting. If the Inquisitor's Leadership is greater than the target's highest Leadership, then the Leadership test is taken with a penalty equal to the different between the two values.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Hammer of the Witches" id="33dd-e1df-084b-9f8d" hidden="false">
      <description>Instead of firing a weapon in the Shooting phase the psyker can take a psychic test to use this power. It does not require LOS to use and may be used if the Inquisitor is in an assault. Roll a D6; this number of enemy psykers must pass a Leadership test or suffer a Perils of the Warp attack, starting with the psyker nearest to the Inquisitor and working outwards. No psyker can be attacked by this more than once.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Hammerhand" id="af4c-0503-c81d-6237" hidden="false">
      <description>This psykic power may be used at the beginning of any Assault phase. On a successful psychic test the psyker doubles their Strength until their next turn. The psyker also counts as having an additional close combat weapon. They may not benefit from any power weapons or other special close combat attacks while this power is active.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="His Will Be Done" id="64e7-7f23-dfff-225c" hidden="false">
      <description>This psychic power is used in the Assault phase before the Inquisitor has made any attacks. If successful, each unsaved wound inflicted by the Inquisitor counts as two for the purposes of determine which side won the assault.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Purgatus" id="dbd0-7c71-0db0-d7be" hidden="false">
      <description>Instead of firing a weapon in the Shooting phase the psyker can take a psychic test to use this power. Choose any enemy model with the Independent Character special rule within 24" of the Inquisitor and within his LOS. Both the Inquisitor and the target roll a D6 and add their Leadership. If the Inquisitor scores higher than the target mode, then the target's Leadership is reduced by 3 for the remainder of the game. This power cannot be used more than once on the same target, and cannot be used on models engaged in an assault.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Scourging" id="5eef-907a-7737-8778" hidden="false">
      <description>Scourging is a psychic power that may be used in the shooting phase instead of firing a weapon. Roll to hit, wound and save as normal, but invulnerable saves may not be taken against wounds caused by Scourging.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Word of the Emperor" id="4420-1044-af7b-ef63" hidden="false">
      <description>This power can be used at the beginning of the enemy Assault phase, even if the psyker is engaged in close combat. All enemy units attempting to charge the psyker or his unit must pass a Leadership test. On a failure they may not assault that turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="The Acolyte" id="d4ae-9c63-c202-23b0" hidden="false">
      <description>An Inquisitor with an Acolyte Henchman may allocate wounds that he suffers to the Acolyte, but may only allocate one wound per phase. This must be done before any saving throws are attempted.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="The Sage" id="a167-544a-1db8-c20a" hidden="false">
      <description>An Inquisitor accompanied by a Sage benefits from +1 BS. If more than one Sage is in his retinue, the Inquisitor or a member of his retinue may re-roll a failed roll to hit during the Shooting Phase.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="The Warrior" id="d536-da50-2f8e-b9cf" hidden="false">
      <description>The Inquisitor gainst +1 WS if he has any warriors in his retinue.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="The Familiar" id="3daa-76d9-c1c5-1e5b" hidden="false">
      <description>An Inquisitor with a Familiar in his retinue benefits from +1 Initiative. For each Familiar in his retinue he may purchase one more psychic power than normally allowed.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="The Penitent" id="95a2-dff1-c457-8f3d" hidden="false">
      <description>If an Inquisitor with a Penitent in his retinue comes under attack from a psychic power of any descript, its energy may be dissipated through the Penitent. The Inquisitor and his retinue benefit from a 4+ save against the effects of any and every psychic power directed against them or include them in its area of effect. If the save is passed the power has no effect.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="The Chirugeon" id="5597-f5b5-ee42-eb49" hidden="false">
      <description>If accompanied by a Chirurgeon, an Inquistory may ignore the first wound that he suffers each turn as long as it was not caused by an attack that causes Instant Death of a close combat attack that allows no Armour save. If he has more than one Chirurgeon he may ignore the first wound even if it was an Instant Death or close combat attack that ignores armour.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Shield of Faith" id="5feb-c54c-9e8a-c500" hidden="false">
      <description>Force weapons used against a model with Shield of Faith lose the ability to instantly kill their target, they simply count as a power weapon instead. Psychic powers targetted against a model with Shield of Faith are nullified and will not work on a D6 roll of 5+.

Minor psychic powers have no effect on Adepta Sororitas units or characters at all, even those used by friendly psykers.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Acts of Faith" id="5b12-9463-d382-9543" hidden="false">
      <description>See the Acts of Faith rule in Codex: Witch Hunters</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Targeter" id="e9b2-e53b-2414-1a22" hidden="false">
      <description>Models equipped with a targeter are allowed to pre-measure the range to a target before they decide who to shoot at in the Shooting phase. This ability must be used after all Guess ranged weapons have been used this turn, otherwise those weapons cannot fire this turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Amphibious" id="65fb-6995-c919-09dd" hidden="false">
      <description>Treat all water features as clear terrain when moving</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Vox-Caster" id="c854-97b0-3b8d-c5d4" hidden="false">
      <description>If a unit containing an Officer has a vo-xcaster, then one squad per turn that also has a vox-caster may use the Leadership ability of the officer regardless of distance. The benefits of standards and trademark items are not conveyed through the vox-caster</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Bionics" id="4053-eb3d-7c9c-241d" hidden="false">
      <description>When a model with bionics is killed, instead place it on its side. Roll a D6 at the start of the next turn: on a roll of 6 the model stands back up with 1 wound, but on any other roll it is removed as a casualty.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="And They Shall Know No Fear" id="f219-56c3-ab1b-6ccd" hidden="false">
      <description>Space Marines automatically regroup as they fall back, even if the squad is reduced to less than 50% by casualties, but not if the squad is out of coherency or there are enemy models within 6". If the enemy advance into them the Space Marines are not destroyed and the new assault is treated in the same way as a sweeping advance (enemy gaining +1 A next turn).</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Simulacrum Imperialis" id="424f-c543-4ada-a802" hidden="false">
      <description>The presence of the Simulacrum Imperialis allows a Faithful unit to roll one extra dice when making a Test of Faith and choose which two dice to use. This may be used once per player turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Servo-skill" id="e0c1-d20d-07d0-d891" hidden="false">
      <description>An Inquisitor with a Familiar in his retinue benefits from +1 Initiative. For each Familiar in his retinue he may purchase one more psychic power than normally allowed.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Rosarius" id="a2e6-23ed-cf18-a4c0" hidden="false">
      <description>4+ Invulnerable save</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Master-crafted" id="0f6e-e675-24a7-6676" hidden="false">
      <description>The bearer may re-roll one failed to hit roll per turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Inquisitorial Mandate" id="3823-309e-5e93-c233" hidden="false">
      <description>A model bearing an Inquisitorial Mandate may reveal it once per battle. This may be done at any time, as long as the model with the Mandate does not move in the turn it is revealed. On the turn the Mandate is revealed, all friendly models with 2D6" receive a +1 Attack bonus for the rest of that turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="VTOL Hover Mode" id="6272-21de-c79d-2f70" hidden="false">
      <description>Rather than leave the table as per normal, the flyer may choose to engage is VTOL Hover mode to remain on the table. It remains stationary, but can turn in any direction to bring its weapons to bear. It may fire all of its weapons.
For the purposes of being fired at, the vehicle counts as a moving Skimmer. It can therefore be fired at using the firer's normal BS. All hits are treated as glancing hits. It can only be attack in close combat by attackers that can fly or have jump packs, in which case it is treated as a moving vehicle.
If the vehicle is immobilised the model is destroyed.
At the end of its own turn, the vehicle may disengage VTOL. It not reverts to being a flyer. It cannot return in the enemy turn immediately afer it leaves the table.</description>
    </rule>
  <rule id="0e13-f956-9067-8648" name="Holy Hatred" hidden="false">
      <description>Celestians gain +1 Attack in the first round of combat in which they were charged.</description>
    </rule>
  <rule name="Psi-shock" id="0c9e-6d60-b658-487e" hidden="false">
      <description>Any psyker that takes an unsaved wound from the stake-crossbow shot suffers the Perils of the Warp in addition to any other effects.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Act of Faith" id="2d2c-92e4-6ee5-21ad" hidden="false">
      <description>An Act of Faith can be attempted immediately before a Sisters of Battle unit acts during a phase; e.g. immediately before the unit moves in the Movement phase, shoots (or runs) in the Shooting phase, or strikes blows in the Assault phase. To attempt an Act of Faith, select the unit and reduce your Faith Point total by 1, then roll a D6 and add the following:




+1 if the unit is led by at least one of the following: Sister Superior, Retributor Superior, Dominion Superior, Seraphim Superior, Celestian Superior or Mistress of Repentance. 




+1 if the unit has been joined by at least one of the following independent characters: Canoness, Ecclesiarchal Confessor, Saint Celestine, Uriah Jacobus or Arch-Confessor Kyrinov. 




+1 if the unit has taken at least 1 casualty. 




Note that all modifiers are cumulative. If the total is less than 5, then the Act of Faith fails. The Faith Point is lost and nothing happens. If the total is equal to or greater than 5, the Act of Faith is successful. The unit immediately gains a bonus and/or special rules until the end of the phase. The nature of the bonus depends upon the unit that is using the Act of Faith, as detailed later.




Independent characters that have the Acts of Faith rule benefit from any bonuses received by the unit they are with when an Act of Faith is used. Similarly, units that have the Acts of Faith rule benefit from any bonuses received by an independent character that has joined the unit when an Act of Faith is used. 
If both a unit and an independent character have an Act of Faith that takes effect in the same phase, you must attempt each Act of Faith separately. 




For example, if a Canoness joins a unit of Celestians then you would require two Faith Points (and two Acts of Faith) to use both the Passion and the Hand of the Emperor Acts of Faith in the Assault phase.</description>
    </rule>
  <rule id="6d3f2230-86ac-8ae9-caaf-086dc960e681-abc68" name="Act of Faith" page="16" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <description>A unit with the Act of Faith special rule can attempt to use its Act of Faith immediately before it acts during a phase; i.e. immediately before the unit moves in the Movement phase, shoots (or runs) in the Shooting phase, or before any blows are stuck (either by friend or foe) in the Assault phase. To do so the unit must take a Leadership test. 

If the test is failed, nothing happens and that unit cannot attempt to use that Act of Faith again for the rest of the battle. If the test is passed, the Act of Faith is successful; unless stated otherwise, all models in the unit will immediately gain a special rule until the end of the current phase. The special rule gained will be listed in that unit's Act of Faith entry, along with which phase(s) the Act of Faith can be attempted in.

Unless stated otherwise, a unit can only attempt to use an Act of Faith once per game and a unit cannot attempt to use more than one Act of Faith in the same phase. A unit can only attempt to use an Act of Faith if it is entirely comprised of models with either the Act of Faith or War Hymns special rules.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="9bf74eeb-9319-52d4-24b4-4024eccfac6e-abc68" name="Martyrdom" page="17" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <description>If a model with the Martyrdom special rule is your Warlord, and that model is removed as a casualty during the battle, all friendly units wholly comprised of models with the Act of Faith special rule automatically pass all Leadership tests until the end of your next turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="102846c2-5cb2-a2bc-5273-7fb66aceaca7-abc68" name="Shield of Faith" page="16" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <description>Models with the Shield of Faith special rule have a 6+ invulnerable save and the Adamantium Will special rule.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="2479a8f3-63b0-4d01-0a1f-673c73c5cb1f-abc68" name="War Hymns" page="25" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <description>A model with this special rule can take a Leadership test at the beginning of each Fight sub-phase in which he is locked in combat. If the test is successful, choose one of the following war hymns to immediately take effect.

The Emperor Protects: The model and his unit re-roll all failed armour and invulnerable saves until the end of the phase.

The Emperor's Strength: The model has the Smash special rule until the end of the phase.

The Righteousness of the Emperor: The model and his unit re-roll failed rolls To Wound until the end of the phase.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="310c-79a4-612a-b222-abc68" name="Fighter Ace" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
    <description>d6 Results
1-2 Crack Shot: Fighter Ace has +1BS
3-4 Evasive Manoeuvers: Improves cover save by1 (to a max cover save of 3+)
5-6 Inspiring Aircraft: Fighter Ace and all friendly units within 12" of the model that are the same Faction have Fearless.</description></rule>
    <rule id="8ef8-513f-b8b9-ef9d-abc68" name="Psi-Shock" page="0" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <description>Any unit with the Pskyer, Brotherhood of Psykers or Psychic Pilot special rules that is hit by a weapon with this special rule suffers the Perils of the Warp in addition to any other damage. </description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules><sharedSelectionEntries><selectionEntry name="Ordo Hereticus Inquisitor Lord" id="27ee-b0a2-0c2a-b518" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" type="unit">
      <categoryLinks>
        <categoryLink name="HQ" id="f198-488a-225e-7c55" hidden="false" primary="true" targetId="ac8d-efba-1884-d3ad" />
        <categoryLink name="Independent Character" id="01ad-66e9-66c2-4749" hidden="false" primary="false" targetId="3c96-248b-affd-e504" />
      </categoryLinks>
      <constraints>
        <constraint id="27f8-6738-af68-38b3" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="force" shared="true" type="max" value="1" />
      </constraints>
      <costs>
        <cost name="Points" typeId="6f18-a8fc-2c5b-9517" value="45" />
      </costs>
      <entryLinks>
        <entryLink name="Psychic Powers" id="9ab4-8e93-66e4-c25f" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" targetId="eb12-8bec-3027-1502" type="selectionEntryGroup" />
        <entryLink name="Witch Hunters Armoury" id="6e48-06de-e8d1-1250" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" targetId="b583-3e64-2ee0-8583" type="selectionEntryGroup" />
        <entryLink name="Inquisitor's Retinue" id="366b-1732-1450-a414" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true" targetId="95b1-bedb-e542-5243" type="selectionEntryGroup" />
      </entryLinks>
      <infoLinks>
